    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Richards returns four weeks after her intake visit. She takes vitamin D3 1971 units every day. She has added yogurt, cheese, and calcium-fortified orange juice, and her three-day food record shows about 1200 mg of calcium a day. She keeps walking and lifting weights and has had no falls. She did not collect the 24-hour urine sample before this visit because she was traveling for three weeks. She saw the endocrinologist this morning. Her balance and strength program with the physical therapist starts next week, and she has a routine dental examination booked next month. She has had no alcohol and no cravings. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Calcium intake</td><td>About 1200 mg a day from food by three-day record</td></tr><tr><td>Vitamin D</td><td>D3 1971 units daily, no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Pending tests</td><td>24-hour urine calcium not yet collected</td></tr><tr><td>Recovery</td><td>No alcohol; no cravings</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

