  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Low bone mass (osteopenia) of the lumbar spine and hip on DXA, lowest T-score -2.3 at the lumbar spine (femoral neck -2.0, total hip -1.7), with a 10-year FRAX risk above the treatment thresholds (major osteoporotic fracture 22 percent, hip 3.6 percent); not osteoporosis by T-score, but meets the AACE 1991 clinical criteria for osteoporosis (low bone mass with a FRAX risk above threshold)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M85.89</td><td>S — Synthetic modern DXA and FRAX classification linked to her publicly described osteopenia (early osteoporosis) after a fall with a hand fracture.</td>
  </tr>
