  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Low bone mass with high fracture risk by FRAX (M85.89)</content>. Lumbar spine T-score -2.3, femoral neck -2.0, and total hip -1.7: low bone mass, not osteoporosis by T-score. FRAX 22 percent for a major osteoporotic fracture and 3.6 percent for hip fracture, both above the treatment thresholds of 20 and 3 percent. Secondary-causes tests are normal apart from vitamin D of 24 ng/mL, now being repleted; the 24-hour urine calcium is outstanding. The endocrinologist agrees that treatment is indicated and recommends zoledronic acid once vitamin D is 30 ng/mL or more and the dental examination is done. [S]<list><item>Continue vitamin D3 1971 units daily and about 1200 mg of calcium a day from food.</item><item>Collect the 24-hour urine calcium before the three-month visit; container and written instructions given again.</item><item>Recheck 25-hydroxyvitamin D, calcium, and creatinine at three months; first zoledronic acid infusion that day if they are in range.</item><item>Routine dental examination next month.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">History of falls (Z91.81)</content>. No falls since intake; balance below normal (tandem stance 8 seconds). [S]<list><item>Balance and strength program with the physical therapist from next week, twice a week for eight weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder in sustained remission (F10.21)</content>. No alcohol or cravings. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in her phone. [S]<list><item>Continue the recovery check at each visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Secondary-causes work-up</td><td>At diagnosis: calcium, albumin, phosphate, magnesium, alkaline phosphatase, creatinine and eGFR, PTH, 25-hydroxyvitamin D, TSH, blood count, and 24-hour urine calcium</td><td>Up to date</td><td>At intake: calcium 9.4 mg/dL, albumin 4.2 g/dL, phosphate 3.5, magnesium 2.0, alkaline phosphatase 84 U/L, creatinine 0.8 mg/dL (eGFR 81), PTH 54 pg/mL, TSH 1.9, hemoglobin 13.3, all normal; 25-hydroxyvitamin D 24 ng/mL, low</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>24-hour urine calcium</td><td>At diagnosis, before starting therapy</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Ordered at intake to be collected before today; not collected because she was traveling. Deviation from the baseline work-up. No harm so far, because no drug has been started. Corrective action: container and instructions given again, and the result is required before the first infusion</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>25-hydroxyvitamin D</td><td>At baseline; after repletion until 30 ng/mL or more; then yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>24 ng/mL at intake; recheck at three months, before the first infusion</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Serum calcium before each intravenous antiresorptive dose</td><td>Before each zoledronic acid dose</td><td>Due</td><td>Planned at three months, before the first infusion</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Bone-turnover marker (fasting serum CTX)</td><td>Baseline, then 3 to 6 months after starting or changing therapy</td><td>Up to date</td><td>560 pg/mL at intake; repeat three months after the first dose</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Central DXA of the spine and hip</td><td>Every 1 to 2 years on therapy until stable, on the same scanner</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Baseline at intake; repeat two years after starting therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Vertebral fracture assessment</td><td>At baseline with a recent low-trauma fracture, height loss of 4 cm or more, or a T-score of -2.5 or lower</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Done at intake for the recent low-trauma fracture: no vertebral fracture</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Standing height by stadiometer</td><td>Yearly; vertebral imaging again if height falls 2 cm or more</td><td>Up to date</td><td>164.0 cm at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall-risk screen</td><td>Yearly, and with any fall</td><td>Up to date</td><td>At intake: Timed Up and Go 11 seconds, tandem stance 8 seconds, chair stand 11; fall with fracture in the past year</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>FRAX 10-year fracture risk</td><td>At baseline and when risk factors change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>22 percent major osteoporotic and 3.6 percent hip at intake; no change in risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Calcium intake assessment</td><td>At baseline and yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About 1200 mg a day from food by three-day record, up from about 800 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Dental examination before an antiresorptive</td><td>Before starting a bisphosphonate or denosumab</td><td>Due</td><td>Routine dental examination booked next month, before the first infusion</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Drug-holiday eligibility</td><td>After 3 yearly zoledronic acid doses or 5 years of an oral bisphosphonate</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No drug started yet</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Denosumab continuity check</td><td>Every 6 months on denosumab</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not on denosumab</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Endocrinology consultation</td><td>When the diagnosis, risk category, or drug choice needs specialist review</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today; treatment indicated; zoledronic acid recommended after vitamin D repletion</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Balance and strength exercise program</td><td>With a history of falls or impaired balance</td><td>Referred</td><td>Physical therapist program begins next week</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Recovery check (alcohol, cravings, stress)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No alcohol; no cravings</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review and safety plan, with the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in her phone</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Total calcium intake of about 1200 mg a day, mostly from food, by the four-week visit. Outcome by 1997-03-10: About 1200 mg a day from food by her own three-day food record [S]</item><item>25-hydroxyvitamin D of 30 ng/mL or more before the first infusion. In progress; target 1997-05-12 [S]</item><item>First zoledronic acid dose by the three-month visit, with normal calcium and kidney function and a dental check done. In progress; target 1997-05-12 [S]</item><item>Complete the eight-week balance and strength program, with no falls through six months. In progress; target 1997-08-11 [S]</item><item>Serum CTX at least 30 percent lower three months after the first dose. In progress; target 1997-08-11 [S]</item><item>Sustained remission from alcohol use disorder throughout the episode. In progress; target 1997-08-11 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, osteoporosis monograph (2026); The clinician&apos;s guide to prevention and treatment of osteoporosis (2022); American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists/American College of Endocrinology Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Postmenopausal Osteoporosis, 2020 Update (2020); Pharmacological Management of Osteoporosis in Postmenopausal Women: An Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2019); STEADI: Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths, and Injuries (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Balance program from next week. Dental examination next month. 24-hour urine collection before the next visit. Bone health review in two months with pre-infusion tests and the first infusion. Next scheduled visit 1997-05-12: three-month bone health review and first zoledronic acid infusion. [S]</paragraph></text>

